│ The issue arises when the prefix variable contains special regex   │
│ characters that are interpreted as regex metacharacters. To        │
│ prevent this, we apply re.escape() to the prefix argument before   │
│ constructing the regex pattern. This ensures that any special      │
│ characters in the prefix are treated as literal characters,        │
│ preserving the intended behavior of the regex. The patch only      │
│ modifies the relevant line in admin/options.py and includes the    │
│ necessary re import to ensure the regex module is available.       │
