│  [original]pk_pattern = re.compile(r'{}-\\d+-{}$'.format(prefix,   │
│  self.model._meta.pk.name))[/original]                             │
│  [patched]pk_pattern =                                             │
│  re.compile(r'{}-\\d+-{}$'.format(re.escape(prefix),               │
│  self.model._meta.pk.name))[/patched]                              │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The patch addresses the issue where the regex pattern in the admin │
│ changeform view is vulnerable to injection of special regex        │
│ characters due to improper escaping of the formset prefix. The     │
│ original code used string formatting to construct the regex        │
│ pattern, which could interpret special characters in the prefix as │
│ regex metacharacters. This leads to incorrect matching or          │
│ potential security vulnerabilities.                                │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix involves:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Escaping the prefix: Using re.escape() around the prefix        │
│    ensures that any special characters in the prefix are treated   │
│    as literal characters in the regex pattern.                     │
│  2 Preserving the original logic: The core logic of the regex      │
│    pattern remains the same, only the escaping of the prefix is    │
│    modified to prevent unintended interpretation.                  │
│                                                                    │
│ The import statement for re is added to ensure the re.escape()     │
│ function is available in the code. This change ensures the regex   │
│ pattern is safely constructed and behaves as intended.             │
